-- title:
--   Reducedness of the fibre of C ⊗_ℤ O over mathfrak m_C
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime number, and let $C$ be a commutative ring which is local and Artinian, whose residue field is finite and of characteristic $\ell$. Let $O$ be a commutative ring in which the principal ideal generated by the image of $\ell$ in $O$, that is $\mathrm{span}\{(\ell : O)\}$, is a maximal ideal. Form the tensor product $C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O$ over the integers, regarded as a $C$-algebra via the structure map $c \mapsto c \otimes 1$, and let $I$ be the ideal of $C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $C$ under that map. The assertion is threefold: the quotient ring $(C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O)/I$ is reduced, i.e. has no nonzero nilpotent elements; it is an Artinian ring; and it is nontrivial, i.e. $0 \neq 1$ in it, so that $I$ is a proper ideal.
--
--   This identifies the fibre of $C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O$ over the closed point of $C$ as a nonzero reduced Artinian ring; concretely this fibre is $\kappa \otimes_{\mathbb F_\ell} (O/\ell O)$ for $\kappa$ the residue field of $C$, a finite separable extension of $\mathbb F_\ell$ tensored with a field of characteristic $\ell$. It is used in the construction of a faithfully flat local extension of an Artin local ring with finite residue field having algebraically closed residue field, where a maximal ideal of $C \otimes_{\mathbb Z} O$ containing the image of $\mathfrak m_C$ must be chosen.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsArtinianRing_isReduced_and_isArtinianRing_tensorProduct_int_quotient_map_maximalIdeal.lean

